cf-class-choice-racket = Rogue's Racket

cf-class-choice-mastermind = Mastermind
cf-class-choice-mastermind-desc = You win by knowing more than your mark. Intelligence is your key attribute, and you are trained in Society. You also choose one of Arcana, Nature, Occultism or Religion. A creature you identify with Recall Knowledge is off-guard to you for 6 seconds, or a minute on a critical success.
cf-class-choice-ruffian = Ruffian
cf-class-choice-ruffian-desc = You hurt people for a living. Strength is your key attribute, and you are trained in Intimidation and medium armor. Sneak Attack works with any simple weapon up to d8, or martial or advanced weapon up to d6. A critical hit with such a weapon on an off-guard creature gets its critical specialization.
cf-class-choice-scoundrel = Scoundrel
cf-class-choice-scoundrel-desc = You talk your way past a guard, then stab it. Charisma is your key attribute, and you are trained in Deception and Diplomacy. A successful Feint leaves the target off-guard to your melee attacks for 6 seconds, and to everyone's on a critical success. With an agile or finesse weapon you can Step for free right after it.
cf-class-choice-thief = Thief
cf-class-choice-thief-desc = You rely on quick hands. Finesse melee weapons and finesse unarmed attacks add your Dexterity to damage when it is higher than your Strength, and you are trained in Thievery.

cf-class-choice-hunters-edge = Hunter's Edge

cf-class-choice-edge-flurry = Flurry
cf-class-choice-edge-flurry-desc = Your multiple attack penalty against your prey is -3 and -6, or -2 and -4 with an agile weapon.
cf-class-choice-edge-outwit = Outwit
cf-class-choice-edge-outwit-desc = +1 circumstance to AC against your prey's attacks. +2 circumstance to Recall Knowledge about it, and to Deception, Intimidation and Stealth checks against it.
cf-class-choice-edge-precision = Precision
cf-class-choice-edge-precision-desc = The first time you hit your prey each turn, you deal 1d8 extra precision damage.

cf-class-feature-weapon-mastery = Fighter Weapon Mastery
cf-class-feature-voice-of-nature = Voice of Nature
cf-class-feature-blessing = Blessing of the Devoted
cf-class-feature-signature-spells = Signature Spells

cf-class-choice-muse = Muse
cf-class-choice-muse-enigma = Enigma
cf-class-choice-muse-enigma-desc = You learn sure strike as a spell and gain the Bardic Lore feat.
cf-class-choice-muse-maestro = Maestro
cf-class-choice-muse-maestro-desc = You learn soothe as a spell and gain the Lingering Composition feat.
cf-class-choice-muse-polymath = Polymath
cf-class-choice-muse-polymath-desc = You gain the Versatile Performance feat. The phantasmal minion spell: TBA
cf-class-choice-muse-warrior = Warrior
cf-class-choice-muse-warrior-desc = You learn fear as a spell and gain the Martial Performance feat.

cf-class-choice-doctrine = Doctrine
cf-class-choice-doctrine-cloistered = Cloistered Cleric
cf-class-choice-doctrine-cloistered-desc = You gain the Domain Initiate feat at level 1, and at level 3 you become an expert in Fortitude saves.
cf-class-choice-doctrine-warpriest = Warpriest
cf-class-choice-doctrine-warpriest-desc = Trained in light and medium armor, expert in Fortitude saves, and Shield Block. At level 3 you are trained in martial weapons. You have Deadly Simplicity, which makes your deity's favored weapon hit harder when it is a simple weapon.

cf-class-choice-order = Druidic Order
cf-class-choice-order-animal = Animal
cf-class-choice-order-animal-desc = You are trained in Athletics, and have the Animal Companion feat: pick the animal on the Pet tab. You can cast heal animal as a focus spell, which heals your companion and other animals.
cf-class-choice-order-leaf = Leaf
cf-class-choice-order-leaf-desc = You are trained in Diplomacy, and have the Leshy Familiar feat: pick the familiar on the Pet tab. You can cast cornucopia as a focus spell, which makes produce that heals whoever eats it.
cf-class-choice-order-storm = Storm
cf-class-choice-order-storm-desc = You are trained in Acrobatics, have the Storm Born feat, and can cast tempest surge as a focus spell.
cf-class-choice-order-untamed = Untamed
cf-class-choice-order-untamed-desc = You are trained in Intimidation, and have the Untamed Form feat and its order spell.

cf-class-choice-school = Arcane School
cf-class-choice-school-ars-grammatica = School of Ars Grammatica
cf-class-choice-school-ars-grammatica-desc = Runes and wards. You know Protective Wards: +1 status to AC for you and allies in an emanation that grows. The extra curriculum slot: TBA
cf-class-choice-school-battle-magic = School of Battle Magic
cf-class-choice-school-battle-magic-desc = You can cast force bolt as a focus spell. The extra curriculum slot: TBA
cf-class-choice-school-boundary = School of the Boundary
cf-class-choice-school-boundary-desc = Spirits and other planes. You know Fortify Summoning: a creature you summoned gains +1 to its checks and AC. The extra curriculum slot: TBA
cf-class-choice-school-civic-wizardry = School of Civic Wizardry
cf-class-choice-school-civic-wizardry-desc = Magic for builders. You know Earthworks: difficult terrain in a 5, 10 or 15-foot burst. The extra curriculum slot: TBA
cf-class-choice-school-mentalism = School of Mentalism
cf-class-choice-school-mentalism-desc = The mind. You know Charming Push: a creature is pushed away from attacking you. The extra curriculum slot: TBA
cf-class-choice-school-protean-form = School of Protean Form
cf-class-choice-school-protean-form-desc = Changing bodies. You know Scramble Body: a creature is sickened, and slowed on a critical failure. The extra curriculum slot: TBA
cf-class-choice-school-unified-theory = School of Unified Magical Theory
cf-class-choice-school-unified-theory-desc = No curriculum. You know Hand of the Apprentice: your melee weapon flies at a creature and back. You gain an extra level 1 wizard class feat. Drain Bonded Item once per spell rank: TBA

cf-class-choice-patron = Patron
cf-class-choice-patron-faiths-flamekeeper = Faith's Flamekeeper
cf-class-choice-patron-faiths-flamekeeper-desc = Divine magic. Trained in Religion. The stoke the heart hex cantrip. Each time you cast a hex, the most hurt of you and your allies within 15 feet of your familiar gains temporary Hit Points equal to 2 plus half your level for 6 seconds. Your familiar learning command: TBA
cf-class-choice-patron-inscribed-one = The Inscribed One
cf-class-choice-patron-inscribed-one-desc = Arcane magic. Trained in Arcana. The discern secrets hex cantrip. Your familiar giving flanking when you cast a hex, and learning runic weapon: TBA
cf-class-choice-patron-resentment = The Resentment
cf-class-choice-patron-resentment-desc = Occult magic. Trained in Occultism. The evil eye hex cantrip. Your familiar prolonging a condition when you cast a hex, and learning enfeeble: TBA
cf-class-choice-patron-silence-in-snow = Silence in Snow
cf-class-choice-patron-silence-in-snow-desc = Primal magic. Trained in Nature. The clinging ice hex cantrip. Each time you cast a hex, ice forms around your familiar: difficult terrain for 6 seconds. Your familiar learning gust of wind: TBA
cf-class-choice-patron-spinner-of-threads = Spinner of Threads
cf-class-choice-patron-spinner-of-threads-desc = Occult magic. Trained in Occultism. The nudge fate hex cantrip. Each time you cast a hex, the enemy nearest your familiar within 15 feet takes -1 status to AC for 6 seconds. Choosing +1 AC for an ally instead, and your familiar learning sure strike: TBA
cf-class-choice-patron-starless-shadow = Starless Shadow
cf-class-choice-patron-starless-shadow-desc = Occult magic. Trained in Occultism. The shroud of night hex cantrip. Your familiar frightening an enemy it is hidden from when you cast a hex, and learning fear: TBA
cf-class-choice-patron-wilding-steward = Wilding Steward
cf-class-choice-patron-wilding-steward-desc = Primal magic. Trained in Nature. The wilding word hex cantrip. Your familiar's keen senses when you cast a hex, and learning summon animal: TBA

cf-class-choice-instinct = Instinct
cf-class-choice-instinctanimal = Animal
cf-class-choice-instinctanimal-desc = Choose an animal. While raging, your unarmed attack is its 1d10 attack: bludgeoning for the ape and the frog, piercing for the rest. The animal's second attack, its grapple, shove or trip trait, and not being able to use weapons while raging: TBA
cf-class-choice-instinctdragon = Dragon
cf-class-choice-instinctdragon-desc = Choose a dragon. Rage adds 4 damage instead of 2, dealt as that dragon's breath type: bludgeoning, poison, fire, spirit, force or mental. It is always that type, where the rules let you choose each Rage.
cf-class-choice-instinctfury = Fury
cf-class-choice-instinctfury-desc = Rage adds 3 damage instead of 2, and you choose one more level 1 barbarian feat.
cf-class-choice-instinctgiant = Giant
cf-class-choice-instinctgiant-desc = Choose a greatsword, a longsword or a warhammer built for a larger creature: it is in your backpack. Raging with it adds 6 damage instead of 2. Whoever holds an oversized weapon is clumsy 1. Its greater Bulk: TBA
cf-class-choice-instinctspirit = Spirit
cf-class-choice-instinctspirit-desc = Rage adds 3 damage instead of 2, dealt as spirit damage. It is always spirit, where the rules let you choose each Rage. Ghost touch: TBA
cf-class-choice-instinctsuperstition = Superstition
cf-class-choice-instinctsuperstition-desc = Rage adds 3 damage instead of 2, or 4 against a creature that cast a spell in the last hour. You have +2 status to saves against magic while raging. When a Rage gives temporary Hit Points you regain as many Hit Points, once per 10 minutes. The anathema against magic, and being frightened by accepting a spell: TBA

cf-class-choice-cause = Cause
cf-class-choice-causedesecration = Desecration
cf-class-choice-causedesecration-desc = Unholy. Selfish Shield: when an enemy in your aura damages you, the damage is 2 + half your level lower, and for 6 seconds your Strikes against it deal 1 more.
cf-class-choice-causegrandeur = Grandeur
cf-class-choice-causegrandeur-desc = Holy. Flash of Grandeur: when an enemy damages an ally, both in your aura, the damage is 2 + your level lower. The revealing light on the attacker: TBA
cf-class-choice-causeiniquity = Iniquity
cf-class-choice-causeiniquity-desc = Unholy. Destructive Vengeance: when an enemy in your aura damages you, you take 1d6 more and it takes 1d6 spirit, 2d6 each from level 5. For 6 seconds your Strikes against it deal 2 more.
cf-class-choice-causejustice = Justice
cf-class-choice-causejustice-desc = Holy. Retributive Strike: when an enemy damages an ally, both in your aura, the damage is 2 + your level lower, and you Strike the enemy if it is in reach.
cf-class-choice-causeliberation = Liberation
cf-class-choice-causeliberation-desc = Holy. Liberating Step: when an enemy damages an ally, both in your aura, the damage is 2 + your level lower and the ally rolls to Escape a grab for free. Setting it off by a grab alone, and the ally's free Step: TBA
cf-class-choice-causeobedience = Obedience
cf-class-choice-causeobedience-desc = Unholy. Iron Command: when an enemy in your aura damages you, it takes 1d6 mental, 2d6 from level 5, and for 6 seconds your Strikes against it deal 1 more. Letting it kneel instead: TBA
cf-class-choice-causeredemption = Redemption
cf-class-choice-causeredemption-desc = Holy. Glimpse of Redemption: when an enemy damages an ally, both in your aura, the damage is 2 + your level lower and the enemy is enfeebled 2 for 6 seconds. Letting it repent instead: TBA

cf-class-choice-devotion = Devotion Spell
cf-class-choice-devotionlayonhands = Lay on Hands
cf-class-choice-devotionlayonhands-desc = Heal a creature with a touch. It costs a Focus Point.
cf-class-choice-devotiontouchofthevoid = Touch of the Void
cf-class-choice-devotiontouchofthevoid-desc = Harm a creature with a touch. It costs a Focus Point.

cf-class-choice-style = Swashbuckler's Style
cf-class-choice-stylebattledancer = Battledancer
cf-class-choice-stylebattledancer-desc = Trained in Performance. You have the Fascinating Performance action, and gain panache when it succeeds. With panache, +1 circumstance to Performance.
cf-class-choice-stylebraggart = Braggart
cf-class-choice-stylebraggart-desc = Trained in Intimidation. You gain panache from Demoralize. With panache, +1 circumstance to Intimidation.
cf-class-choice-stylefencer = Fencer
cf-class-choice-stylefencer-desc = Trained in Deception. You gain panache from Feint and from Create a Diversion. With panache, +1 circumstance to Deception.
cf-class-choice-stylegymnast = Gymnast
cf-class-choice-stylegymnast-desc = Trained in Athletics. You gain panache from a successful Grapple, Shove or Disarm. With panache, +1 circumstance to Athletics. From Reposition: TBA
cf-class-choice-stylerascal = Rascal
cf-class-choice-stylerascal-desc = Trained in Thievery. You have the Dirty Trick action, and gain panache when it succeeds. With panache, +1 circumstance to Thievery.
cf-class-choice-stylewit = Wit
cf-class-choice-stylewit-desc = Trained in Diplomacy. You have the Bon Mot action, and gain panache when it succeeds. With panache, +1 circumstance to Diplomacy.

cf-class-choice-methodology = Methodology
cf-class-choice-methodalchemicalsciences = Alchemical Sciences
cf-class-choice-methodalchemicalsciences-desc = Trained in Crafting. Versatile vials, and the feat and formulas: TBA
cf-class-choice-methodempiricism = Empiricism
cf-class-choice-methodempiricism-desc = Trained in an Intelligence skill of your choice. You have the That's Odd feat, and Expeditious Inspection: a free Recall Knowledge once every 10 minutes. Its free Seek or Sense Motive: TBA
cf-class-choice-methodforensicmedicine = Forensic Medicine
cf-class-choice-methodforensicmedicine-desc = Trained in Medicine, with Battle Medicine, which restores your level more. Forensic Acumen: TBA
cf-class-choice-methodinterrogation = Interrogation
cf-class-choice-methodinterrogation-desc = Trained in Diplomacy. You have Pointed Question: a Diplomacy check against Will that leaves the creature off-guard to you for 6 seconds. No Cause for Alarm: TBA

cf-class-choice-research-field = Research Field
cf-class-choice-fieldbomber = Bomber
cf-class-choice-fieldbomber-desc = Your bombs never splash you or your allies, and Quick Vial can make cold, electricity or fire vials. From level 5 a bomb's splash is at least your Intelligence modifier. The two bomb formulas: TBA
cf-class-choice-fieldchirurgeon = Chirurgeon
cf-class-choice-fieldchirurgeon-desc = Crafting stands in for Medicine, for Treat Wounds and Battle Medicine, and Quick Vial can make a healing vial that restores 1d6 Hit Points, 2d6 from level 4. The two elixir formulas: TBA
cf-class-choice-fieldmutagenist = Mutagenist
cf-class-choice-fieldmutagenist-desc = You study transformation. There are no mutagens yet: TBA
cf-class-choice-fieldtoxicologist = Toxicologist
cf-class-choice-fieldtoxicologist-desc = Quick Vial can make a poison vial. From level 5 you have poison resistance equal to half your level. Injury poisons on a weapon: TBA

cf-class-choice-bloodline = Bloodline
cf-class-choice-bloodlineaberrant = Aberrant
cf-class-choice-bloodlineaberrant-desc = Occult spells. Trained in Intimidation and Occultism. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: an enemy the spell reaches takes -1 status to Will saves for 6 seconds, or else you get +2. Its bloodline spell, tentacular limbs: TBA
cf-class-choice-bloodlineangelic = Angelic
cf-class-choice-bloodlineangelic-desc = Divine spells. Trained in Diplomacy and Religion. The angelic halo focus spell. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: you, or the ally the spell was for, get +1 status to saves for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedemonic = Demonic
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedemonic-desc = Divine spells. Trained in Intimidation and Religion. The glutton's jaws focus spell. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: an enemy the spell reaches takes -1 status to AC for 6 seconds, or else you get +2 status to Intimidation. Its cantrip, caustic blast: TBA
cf-class-choice-bloodlinediabolic = Diabolic
cf-class-choice-bloodlinediabolic-desc = Divine spells. Trained in Deception and Religion. The diabolic edict focus spell. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: an enemy the spell reaches takes 1 fire damage per spell rank, or else you get +2 status to Deception for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedraconicarcane = Draconic (Arcane)
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedraconicarcane-desc = Arcane spells. Trained in Intimidation and Arcana. The flurry of claws focus spell, with force damage. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: you, or the ally the spell was for, get +1 status to AC for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedraconicdivine = Draconic (Divine)
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedraconicdivine-desc = Divine spells. Trained in Intimidation and Religion. The flurry of claws focus spell, with spirit damage. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: you, or the ally the spell was for, get +1 status to AC for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedraconicoccult = Draconic (Occult)
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedraconicoccult-desc = Occult spells. Trained in Intimidation and Occultism. The flurry of claws focus spell, with mental damage. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: you, or the ally the spell was for, get +1 status to AC for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedraconicprimal = Draconic (Primal)
cf-class-choice-bloodlinedraconicprimal-desc = Primal spells. Trained in Intimidation and Nature. The flurry of claws focus spell, with fire damage. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: you, or the ally the spell was for, get +1 status to AC for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-bloodlineelemental = Elemental
cf-class-choice-bloodlineelemental-desc = Primal spells. Trained in Intimidation and Nature. The elemental toss focus spell. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: an enemy the spell reaches takes 1 fire damage per spell rank, or else you get +2 status to Intimidation for 6 seconds. Choosing another element than fire: TBA
cf-class-choice-bloodlinefey = Fey
cf-class-choice-bloodlinefey-desc = Primal spells. Trained in Deception and Nature. The faerie dust focus spell. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: you are concealed for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-bloodlinehag = Hag
cf-class-choice-bloodlinehag-desc = Occult spells. Trained in Deception and Occultism. The jealous hex focus spell. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: you gain temporary Hit Points equal to the spell's rank for 6 seconds. The mental damage to whoever hurts you first, and its rank 1 spell, illusory disguise: TBA
cf-class-choice-bloodlineimperial = Imperial
cf-class-choice-bloodlineimperial-desc = Arcane spells. Trained in Arcana and Society. The ancestral memories focus spell. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: you get +1 status to AC for 6 seconds. Choosing saves instead: TBA
cf-class-choice-bloodlineundead = Undead
cf-class-choice-bloodlineundead-desc = Divine spells. Trained in Intimidation and Religion. Blood magic, when you cast a bloodline spell or a spell your bloodline gave you from a slot: an enemy the spell reaches takes 1 void damage per spell rank, or else you gain temporary Hit Points equal to the rank for 6 seconds. Its bloodline spell, undeath's blessing: TBA

cf-class-choice-mystery = Mystery
cf-class-choice-mysteryancestors = Ancestors
cf-class-choice-mysteryancestors-desc = Trained in Society. The ancestral touch revelation spell, and Whispers of Weakness. Curse: you are clumsy at your cursebound value. Its rank 1 spell: TBA
cf-class-choice-mysterybattle = Battle
cf-class-choice-mysterybattle-desc = Trained in Athletics. The weapon trance revelation spell, and Oracular Warning. Curse: at cursebound 2, -1 status to saves against magic. Its weakness to spells at cursebound 1: TBA
cf-class-choice-mysterybones = Bones
cf-class-choice-mysterybones-desc = Trained in Medicine. The soul siphon revelation spell, and Nudge the Scales. Curse: weakness 2 to vitality and void, and at cursebound 2, -1 status to Fortitude. Being hurt by both energies, and its rank 1 spell: TBA
cf-class-choice-mysterycosmos = Cosmos
cf-class-choice-mysterycosmos-desc = Trained in Nature. The spray of stars revelation spell, and Oracular Warning. Curse: you are enfeebled at your cursebound value, and that much easier to Shove, Trip and Grapple. Its rank 1 spell: TBA
cf-class-choice-mysteryflames = Flames
cf-class-choice-mysteryflames-desc = Trained in Acrobatics. Foretell Harm. Curse: each time your cursebound value rises you catch fire, for persistent fire damage equal to it. Its revelation spell, incendiary aura: TBA
cf-class-choice-mysterylife = Life
cf-class-choice-mysterylife-desc = Trained in Medicine. The life link revelation spell, and Nudge the Scales. Curse: healing spells restore your level less to you, for each point of cursebound.
cf-class-choice-mysterylore = Lore
cf-class-choice-mysterylore-desc = Trained in Occultism. The brain drain revelation spell, and Whispers of Weakness. Curse: a status penalty to Perception and Will saves equal to your cursebound value. A Lore skill and its rank 1 spell: TBA
cf-class-choice-mysterytempest = Tempest
cf-class-choice-mysterytempest-desc = Trained in Nature. The tempest touch revelation spell, and Foretell Harm. Curse: weakness 2 to electricity. The penalty to ranged attacks at cursebound 2: TBA

cf-reaction-opportune-riposte = Opportune Riposte
cf-class-choice-devotionshieldsofthespirit = Shields of the Spirit
cf-class-choice-devotionshieldsofthespirit-desc = Raise your shield. For 6 seconds, allies in your aura have +1 status bonus to AC, and an enemy that attacks one takes 1d4 spirit damage. It costs a Focus Point.
cf-reaction-selfish-shield = Selfish Shield
cf-reaction-flash-of-grandeur = Flash of Grandeur
cf-reaction-destructive-vengeance = Destructive Vengeance
cf-reaction-retributive-strike = Retributive Strike
cf-reaction-liberating-step = Liberating Step
cf-reaction-iron-command = Iron Command
cf-reaction-glimpse-of-redemption = Glimpse of Redemption

cf-class-choice-hybrid-study = Hybrid Study
cf-class-choice-studyalooffirmament = Aloof Firmament
cf-class-choice-studyalooffirmament-desc = You have the Cat Fall feat. Its conflux spell costs a Focus Point and recharges Spellstrike: Sky Laughs at Waves, a 25-foot rush to an enemy and a melee Strike. In Arcane Cascade, lighter jumps that set off no reactions, and a harder sword Strike after one: TBA
cf-class-choice-studyinexorableiron = Inexorable Iron
cf-class-choice-studyinexorableiron-desc = Entering Arcane Cascade with a melee weapon held in both hands gives temporary Hit Points equal to half your level for a minute. Its conflux spell costs a Focus Point and recharges Spellstrike: Thunderous Strike, a two-handed Strike that adds sonic damage. The temporary Hit Points again each turn, and the cone that knocks creatures prone: TBA
cf-class-choice-studylaughingshadow = Laughing Shadow
cf-class-choice-studylaughingshadow-desc = In Arcane Cascade, +5 feet status bonus to Speed, or +10 with no armor. Its conflux spell costs a Focus Point and recharges Spellstrike: Dimensional Assault, a 15-foot rush to an enemy and a melee Strike. More damage against an off-guard creature with a hand free: TBA
cf-class-choice-studyresurgentmaelstrom = Resurgent Maelstrom
cf-class-choice-studyresurgentmaelstrom-desc = Improvised weapons with no penalty, a larger die and extra traits: TBA. Its conflux spell: TBA
cf-class-choice-studysparklingtarge = Sparkling Targe
cf-class-choice-studysparklingtarge-desc = You have Shield Block. While your shield is raised, +2 circumstance to saves against magic. Its conflux spell costs a Focus Point and recharges Spellstrike: Shielding Strike, which raises your shield and Strikes. The rules ask for Arcane Cascade and use the shield's own bonus. Blocking magical damage: TBA
cf-class-choice-studystarlitspan = Starlit Span
cf-class-choice-studystarlitspan-desc = Its conflux spell costs a Focus Point and recharges Spellstrike: Shooting Star, a ranged Strike that ignores concealment. Spellstrike with a ranged weapon: TBA
cf-class-choice-studytwistingtree = Twisting Tree
cf-class-choice-studytwistingtree-desc = Its conflux spell costs a Focus Point and recharges Spellstrike: Spinning Staff, a staff Strike and a second at another enemy in reach. A staff in one hand being agile with a d6 die, and parry, reach and trip in both hands: TBA
cf-class-choice-studytwofoldtine = Twofold Tine
cf-class-choice-studytwofoldtine-desc = Its conflux spell costs a Focus Point and recharges Spellstrike: Force Fling, a melee Strike at a creature up to 15 feet away. Its damage as force, and the stance's extra damage for your other weapon: TBA
cf-class-choice-studyunfurlingbrocade = Unfurling Brocade
cf-class-choice-studyunfurlingbrocade-desc = A length of cloth becomes a bladed scarf you can wield in one hand: TBA. Its conflux spell: TBA
cf-class-choice-studyvolatilespark = Volatile Spark
cf-class-choice-studyvolatilespark-desc = Spellstrike with a firearm, inside its first range increment, and reloading as you enter Arcane Cascade: TBA. Its conflux spell, Booming Blast: TBA

cf-class-choice-implement = First Implement

cf-class-choice-way = Gunslinger's Way
cf-class-choice-waydrifter = Way of the Drifter
cf-class-choice-waydrifter-desc = Trained in Acrobatics. Reloading Strike: a Strike with the one-handed melee weapon in your other hand, or your fist, and your firearm or crossbow is loaded with no hand free. Into the Fray: as a fight begins you draw a one-handed firearm or crossbow and a one-handed melee weapon from your belt, back or neck. Its free Stride: TBA
cf-class-choice-waypistolero = Way of the Pistolero
cf-class-choice-waypistolero-desc = Trained in Deception or Intimidation, your choice. Raconteur's Reload: Demoralize and load. Ten Paces: as a fight begins you draw a one-handed firearm or crossbow, and for 3 seconds a Step costs nothing. Create a Diversion with the reload, and the bonus to initiative: TBA
cf-class-choice-waysniper = Way of the Sniper
cf-class-choice-waysniper-desc = Trained in Stealth. Covered Reload: Hide and load. One Shot, One Kill: as a fight begins you draw a firearm or crossbow, and your first Strike with one that hits deals 1d6 more. Take Cover with the reload: TBA
cf-class-choice-wayspellshot = Way of the Spellshot
cf-class-choice-wayspellshot-desc = Trained in Arcana. Thoughtful Reload: Recall Knowledge about an enemy and load. Energy Shot: as a fight begins you draw a firearm or crossbow, and your first three Strikes with one deal 1 fire damage per weapon die. Choosing acid, cold or electricity instead: TBA
cf-class-choice-waytriggerbrand = Way of the Triggerbrand
cf-class-choice-waytriggerbrand-desc = Trained in Thievery. Combination weapons do not exist yet: TBA
cf-class-choice-wayvanguard = Way of the Vanguard
cf-class-choice-wayvanguard-desc = Trained in Athletics. Clear a Path: Shove and load. Living Fortification: as a fight begins you draw a firearm or crossbow and hold it as a guard, +1 AC for 6 seconds.

cf-class-choice-innovation = Innovation

cf-class-choice-conscious = Conscious Mind
cf-class-choice-consciousthedistantgrasp = The Distant Grasp
cf-class-choice-consciousthedistantgrasp-desc = Psi cantrips: telekinetic projectile and telekinetic rend. You also know kinetic ram. Telekinetic hand: TBA
cf-class-choice-conscioustheinfiniteeye = The Infinite Eye
cf-class-choice-conscioustheinfiniteeye-desc = Psi cantrips: detect magic, guidance and glimpse weakness. You also know sure strike. Amped detect magic gives +1 status to saves against magic for 18 seconds; amped guidance guides saves, skills and Perception too.
cf-class-choice-conscioustheoscillatingwave = The Oscillating Wave
cf-class-choice-conscioustheoscillatingwave-desc = Psi cantrips: frostbite, ignition and thermal stasis. You also know breathe fire. Conservation of Energy: the first of these you cast keeps its energy, and each one after deals the other, fire or cold, until a minute passes with none cast.
cf-class-choice-consciousthesilentwhisper = The Silent Whisper
cf-class-choice-consciousthesilentwhisper-desc = Psi cantrips: daze, at any range your spell reaches, and forbidden thought, a lock against Striking or casting. Message: TBA
cf-class-choice-consciousthetangibledream = The Tangible Dream
cf-class-choice-consciousthetangibledream-desc = Psi cantrips: figment, shield and imaginary weapon. Amped figment leaves the enemy beside it off-guard; amped shield lasts a minute and blocks 15. Its rank 1 spell, dizzying colors: TBA
cf-class-choice-conscioustheunboundstep = The Unbound Step
cf-class-choice-conscioustheunboundstep-desc = Psi cantrips: phase bolt and warp step, which is +5 feet to your Speed, +10 amped. Distortion lens and thoughtful gift: TBA

cf-class-choice-subconscious = Subconscious Mind
cf-class-choice-subconsciousemotionalacceptance = Emotional Acceptance
cf-class-choice-subconsciousemotionalacceptance-desc = Charisma is your key attribute. Restore the Mind heals an ally while you are Unleashed, and gives them +1 status to saves against mental effects for 12 seconds. The rules offer one or the other.
cf-class-choice-subconsciousgatheredlore = Gathered Lore
cf-class-choice-subconsciousgatheredlore-desc = Intelligence is your key attribute. Recall the Teachings, while you are Unleashed, is an Occultism check that Aids every ally within 30 feet at once.
cf-class-choice-subconsciousprecisediscipline = Precise Discipline
cf-class-choice-subconsciousprecisediscipline-desc = Intelligence is your key attribute. Calculate Threats gives +2 to AC and Reflex while you are Unleashed.
cf-class-choice-subconsciouswanderingreverie = Wandering Reverie
cf-class-choice-subconsciouswanderingreverie-desc = Charisma is your key attribute. Fade into Daydreams conceals you while you are Unleashed.

cf-class-choice-fascination = Grim Fascination
cf-class-choice-fascinationblood = Blood
cf-class-choice-fascinationblood-desc = You know Blood Infusion, and regain 1 Hit Point when a thrall is destroyed, 2 from level 5.
cf-class-choice-fascinationbone = Bone
cf-class-choice-fascinationbone-desc = You know Bone Spear, and your thralls have 5 feet more Speed.
cf-class-choice-fascinationflesh = Flesh
cf-class-choice-fascinationflesh-desc = You know Dead Weight, and a destroyed thrall leaves dead flesh where it fell, difficult terrain for 10 minutes. Dead Weight's slowed: TBA
cf-class-choice-fascinationspirit = Spirit
cf-class-choice-fascinationspirit-desc = You know Life Tap, and your thralls deal spirit damage. The rules let you choose void instead with each Strike.

cf-class-choice-fatal-method = Fatal Method
cf-class-choice-methodpuppeteer = Puppeteer
cf-class-choice-methodpuppeteer-desc = Create Thrall makes one more thrall. Consume Thrall, free and once a day: with every Focus Point spent, a thrall within 30 feet is destroyed and you regain 1. The rules keep that point for grave spells.
cf-class-choice-methodreaper = Reaper
cf-class-choice-methodreaper-desc = Trained in martial weapons and medium armor. Thrall Teamwork: after Create Thrall you make a free melee Strike at an enemy in your reach that stands beside one of your thralls.

cf-class-choice-practice = Animistic Practice
cf-class-choice-practiceliturgist = Liturgist
cf-class-choice-practiceliturgist-desc = You can use Circle of Spirits, and have one more Focus Point.
cf-class-choice-practicemedium = Medium
cf-class-choice-practicemedium-desc = Relinquish Control: TBA
cf-class-choice-practiceseer = Seer
cf-class-choice-practiceseer-desc = +1 status to saves against undead. The same bonus to AC, and sensing spirits: TBA
cf-class-choice-practiceshaman = Shaman
cf-class-choice-practiceshaman-desc = A spirit familiar: TBA
cf-reaction-intercept-attack = Intercept Attack

cf-class-choice-second-implement = Second Implement (level 5)
cf-class-choice-implementamulet = Amulet
cf-class-choice-implementamulet-desc = Holding it, when the enemy you Exploited would damage you or an ally within 15 feet, your reaction takes 2 + your level off the damage.
cf-class-choice-secondimplementamulet = Amulet
cf-class-choice-secondimplementamulet-desc = Gained at level 5. Holding it, when the enemy you Exploited would damage you or an ally within 15 feet, your reaction takes 2 + your level off the damage.
cf-class-choice-implementbell = Bell
cf-class-choice-implementbell-desc = Ring Bell, a reaction: holding it, when the enemy you Exploited damages you or an ally within 30 feet, it rolls Will against your class DC or is enfeebled 1 for 6 seconds, 2 on a critical failure. Its answer to a spell, and choosing clumsy: TBA
cf-class-choice-secondimplementbell = Bell
cf-class-choice-secondimplementbell-desc = Ring Bell, a reaction: holding it, when the enemy you Exploited damages you or an ally within 30 feet, it rolls Will against your class DC or is enfeebled 1 for 6 seconds, 2 on a critical failure. Its answer to a spell, and choosing clumsy: TBA
cf-class-choice-implementcenser = Censer
cf-class-choice-implementcenser-desc = A cloud of smoke around you: TBA
cf-class-choice-secondimplementcenser = Censer
cf-class-choice-secondimplementcenser-desc = Gained at level 5. A cloud of smoke around you: TBA
cf-class-choice-implementchalice = Chalice
cf-class-choice-implementchalice-desc = Drain the Chalice heals you or an adjacent ally 3 Hit Points per level, and refills in 10 minutes. Sip from the Chalice gives temporary Hit Points equal to your level, 3 at least, for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-secondimplementchalice = Chalice
cf-class-choice-secondimplementchalice-desc = Drain the Chalice heals you or an adjacent ally 3 Hit Points per level, and refills in 10 minutes. Sip from the Chalice gives temporary Hit Points equal to your level, 3 at least, for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-implementlantern = Lantern
cf-class-choice-implementlantern-desc = Holding it, you and allies within 20 feet have +1 status bonus to Perception, and it gives light. Revealing the unseen: TBA
cf-class-choice-secondimplementlantern = Lantern
cf-class-choice-secondimplementlantern-desc = Gained at level 5. Holding it, you and allies within 20 feet have +1 status bonus to Perception, and it gives light. Revealing the unseen: TBA
cf-class-choice-implementmirror = Mirror
cf-class-choice-implementmirror-desc = Mirror's Reflection, a second you: TBA
cf-class-choice-secondimplementmirror = Mirror
cf-class-choice-secondimplementmirror-desc = Gained at level 5. Mirror's Reflection, a second you: TBA
cf-class-choice-implementregalia = Regalia
cf-class-choice-implementregalia-desc = Holding it, +1 circumstance bonus to Deception, Diplomacy and Intimidation, and you and allies within 15 feet have +1 status bonus to saves against fear.
cf-class-choice-secondimplementregalia = Regalia
cf-class-choice-secondimplementregalia-desc = Gained at level 5. Holding it, +1 circumstance bonus to Deception, Diplomacy and Intimidation, and you and allies within 15 feet have +1 status bonus to saves against fear.
cf-class-choice-implementshield = Shield
cf-class-choice-implementshield-desc = A warding shield, and you can Shield Block with it. Surviving when it would be destroyed: TBA
cf-class-choice-secondimplementshield = Shield
cf-class-choice-secondimplementshield-desc = Gained at level 5. A warding shield, and you can Shield Block with it. Surviving when it would be destroyed: TBA
cf-class-choice-implementtome = Tome
cf-class-choice-implementtome-desc = Holding it, +1 circumstance bonus to Recall Knowledge. You are trained in two skills of your choice for the day: change them on the character sheet's Daily tab. Becoming expert in them at levels 3 and 5: TBA
cf-class-choice-secondimplementtome = Tome
cf-class-choice-secondimplementtome-desc = Gained at level 5. Holding it, +1 circumstance bonus to Recall Knowledge. Temporary skills from it: TBA
cf-class-choice-implementwandfire = Wand (Fire)
cf-class-choice-implementwandfire-desc = Fling Magic: 3d4 fire within 60 feet, basic Reflex, for 2 actions. Its boosted version deals d6s, once every 12 seconds.
cf-class-choice-secondimplementwandfire = Wand (Fire)
cf-class-choice-secondimplementwandfire-desc = Fling Magic: 3d4 fire within 60 feet, basic Reflex, for 2 actions. Its boosted version deals d6s, once every 12 seconds.
cf-class-choice-implementwandcold = Wand (Cold)
cf-class-choice-implementwandcold-desc = Fling Magic: 3d4 cold within 60 feet, basic Reflex, for 2 actions. Its boosted version deals d6s, once every 12 seconds.
cf-class-choice-secondimplementwandcold = Wand (Cold)
cf-class-choice-secondimplementwandcold-desc = Fling Magic: 3d4 cold within 60 feet, basic Reflex, for 2 actions. Its boosted version deals d6s, once every 12 seconds.
cf-class-choice-implementwandelectricity = Wand (Electricity)
cf-class-choice-implementwandelectricity-desc = Fling Magic: 3d4 electricity within 60 feet, basic Reflex, for 2 actions. Its boosted version deals d6s, once every 12 seconds.
cf-class-choice-secondimplementwandelectricity = Wand (Electricity)
cf-class-choice-secondimplementwandelectricity-desc = Fling Magic: 3d4 electricity within 60 feet, basic Reflex, for 2 actions. Its boosted version deals d6s, once every 12 seconds.
cf-class-choice-implementweapon = Weapon
cf-class-choice-implementweapon-desc = Any one-handed weapon in your hand counts as your implement. When the enemy you Exploited runs out of your reach, your reaction Strikes it.
cf-class-choice-secondimplementweapon = Weapon
cf-class-choice-secondimplementweapon-desc = Gained at level 5. Any one-handed weapon in your hand counts as your implement. When the enemy you Exploited runs out of your reach, your reaction Strikes it.
cf-reaction-amulets-abeyance = Amulet's Abeyance
cf-reaction-implements-interruption = Implement's Interruption

cf-class-choice-tactic-first = First Tactic
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-pincerattack = Pincer Attack
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-pincerattack-desc = 1 action. Enemies next to any of your squad are off-guard to the whole squad for 6 seconds.
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-reload = Reload!
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-reload-desc = 1 action. Everyone in your squad loads the weapon they are holding.
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-shieldsup = Shields Up!
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-shieldsup-desc = 1 action. Everyone in your squad raises a held shield.
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-strikehard = Strike Hard!
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-strikehard-desc = 2 actions. A member of your squad Strikes the nearest enemy in their reach.
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-takedown = Tactical Takedown
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-takedown-desc = 2 actions. An enemy with two of your squad next to it must save or fall prone.
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-defensiveretreat = Defensive Retreat
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-defensiveretreat-desc = 2 actions. Your squad gets +10 feet Speed for 3 seconds. Stepping for them: TBA
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-gathertome = Gather to Me!
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-gathertome-desc = 1 action. Your squad gets +10 feet Speed for 3 seconds. Striding for them: TBA
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-doubleteam = Double Team
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-doubleteam-desc = 2 actions. The nearest squad member in reach of an enemy Shoves it, and if it lands in another member's reach, that one Strikes it.
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-coordinatingmaneuvers = Coordinating Maneuvers
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-coordinatingmaneuvers-desc = 1 action. The nearest squad member in reach of an enemy Repositions it 5 feet away from you, 10 on a critical success. The free Step: TBA
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-endit = End It!
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-endit-desc = 2 actions. Only when your side outnumbers the enemy and your squad dropped one in the last 6 seconds. Enemies within 10 feet of a squad member save Will or are frightened 1, frightened 2 on a critical failure. Fleeing does not exist here, so frightened stands in: TBA
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-mountaineeringtraining = Mountaineering Training
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-mountaineeringtraining-desc = 1 action. Your squad has a climb Speed for 6 seconds. Warfare Lore to Climb: TBA
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-navaltraining = Naval Training
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-navaltraining-desc = 1 action. Your squad has a swim Speed for 6 seconds. Water does not exist yet: TBA
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-passageoflines = Passage of Lines
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-passageoflines-desc = 1 action. Squad members standing beside each other trade places.
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-protectivescreen = Protective Screen
cf-class-choice-tactic-first-protectivescreen-desc = 1 action. A squad member's spells and ranged attacks set off no reactions for 6 seconds. The Stride to them: TBA

